(4) GATE VERDICT: HONEST-NEGATIVE  (fails on every axis)
    [FAIL] DPLR recall@1 does NOT beat plain cosine (== within noise; delta-rule decorrelation is a no-op
           on 61 near-orthogonal content-bearing vectors).
    [FAIL] DPLR recall@1 (73.8-83.6%) does NOT reach the incumbent ~85% / 88.5% paraphrase bar.
    [FAIL] foreign-reject via a global cosine/DPLR tau is not clean (AUROC ~0.42-0.50) -- content-bearing
           cosine cannot separate topically-adjacent foreign; the deployed L5+attr-gate path is better.
    [FAIL] erase is not lossless (9-10/61 neighbor collateral) vs A1's non-destructive supersede.

    MECHANISM READ: On content-bearing bge vectors the 61 facts are already near-orthogonal, so the DPLR
    erase-then-write delta rule reduces to plain cosine ranking -- it adds nothing. DPLR's ONLY distinctive
    value is editable erase/overwrite, and even that is not lossless here (perturbs correlated neighbors),
    whereas A1's deterministic supersede/dedup already provides clean, lossless overwrite. DPLR is therefore
    REDUNDANT for our memory path and does not beat the deployed L5-direct+tau incumbent. B5 CLOSED-NEGATIVE.

